[patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-018-saga-pattern.md#problem-1-two-phase-commit-is-not-viable]

#### Problem 1: Two-Phase Commit is Not Viable

**Traditional 2PC Approach (Not Used)**:

```csharp
// Hypothetical 2PC coordinator (NOT IMPLEMENTED - shown for illustration only)
public async Task<ClaimResult> AdjudicateClaim2PC(Claim claim)
{
    var transactionCoordinator = new DistributedTransactionCoordinator();

    try
    {
        // PREPARE PHASE - Ask all services if they can commit
        transactionCoordinator.Begin();

        var eligibilityResult = await _eligibilityService.PrepareEligibilityCheck(claim.MemberId);
        transactionCoordinator.Register(eligibilityResult);

        var benefitsResult = await _benefitsService.PrepareBenefitsValidation(claim);
        transactionCoordinator.Register(benefitsResult);

        var pricingResult = await _pricingService.PreparePriceCalculation(claim);
        transactionCoordinator.Register(pricingResult);

        var paymentResult = await _paymentService.PreparePayment(claim);
        transactionCoordinator.Register(paymentResult);

        // COMMIT PHASE - Tell all services to commit
        if (transactionCoordinator.CanCommit())
        {
            await transactionCoordinator.CommitAll();
            return ClaimResult.Approved(claim.ClaimId);
        }
        else
        {
            await transactionCoordinator.RollbackAll();
            return ClaimResult.Denied(claim.ClaimId);
        }
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        // Coordinator failure during PREPARE phase - all participants blocked
        // Resources locked in eligibility service, benefits service, pricing service
        // Cannot proceed, cannot rollback - DEADLOCK

        throw new DistributedTransactionException(
            "Coordinator failed during 2PC. All participants blocked.", ex);
    }
}
```

**Why 2PC Fails in Healthcare Microservices**:

1. **Blocking During Coordinator Failure**:
   - If coordinator fails after sending PREPARE to 3 of 5 services, those 3 services have resources locked indefinitely
   - In claims processing at 500K/day, even 5-minute coordinator recovery blocks 1,700+ claims
   - Healthcare SLA requires <30 second recovery, impossible with 2PC

2. **Cascading Availability Impact**:
   - 2PC requires ALL services available simultaneously
   - If benefits service is down (during deployment, network issue), entire claims adjudication stops
   - With 8 services in the workflow, availability = 0.999^8 = 0.992 = 99.2% (below 99.9% SLA)

3. **Performance Degradation**:
   - 2PC latency: 5 services × (prepare + commit) × 50ms network latency = 500ms minimum overhead
   - Without 2PC: asynchronous saga completes in 200ms average (2.5x faster)

4. **Technology Limitations**:
   - MongoDB doesn't support XA transactions (network service cannot participate in 2PC)
   - Elasticsearch doesn't support distributed transactions (directory service cannot participate)
   - Redis has limited transaction support (caching layer excluded from 2PC)

